23907 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186523646 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523907 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e8508966-666d-5767-9f3e-6f1a14747298" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523933 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186523828 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523933 #edb/ref 1069 "q-122989" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523933 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523933 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $P=\\{{z}_{0},{z}_{1},…,{z}_{q}\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[-4,-2].$ If $Δ{z}_{k}={z}_{k}-{z}_{k-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523933 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1bfa03d7-9352-51b2-9697-231f8df40ac5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523933 #edb/ref 1074 "We can simplify the given summation as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k} & =({z}_{1}+{z}_{0})Δ{z}_{1}+({z}_{2}+{z}_{1})Δ{z}_{2}+⋯+({z}_{q}+{z}_{q-1})Δ{z}_{n} \\\\  & =({z}_{1}+{z}_{0})({z}_{1}-{z}_{0})+({z}_{2}+{z}_{1})({z}_{2}-{z}_{1})+⋯+({z}_{q}+{z}_{q-1})({z}_{q}-{z}_{q-1}) \\\\  & =({z}_{1}^{2}-{z}_{0}^{2})+({z}_{2}^{2}-{z}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({z}_{q}^{2}-{z}_{q-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{z}_{1}^{2}}-{z}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{z}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{z}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({z}_{q}^{2}-\\cancel{{z}_{q-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{z}_{0}^{2}+{z}_{q}^{2} \\\\  & ={z}_{q}^{2}-{z}_{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${z}_{0}=-4$ and ${z}_{q}=-2$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k} & ={z}_{q}^{2}-{z}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(-2)^{2}-(-4)^{2} \\\\  & =-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523942 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186523898 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523942 #edb/ref 1069 "q-122969" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523942 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523942 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $P=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[2,8].$ If $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523942 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "28824d9b-0c0b-596c-9f64-75c745081e48" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523942 #edb/ref 1074 "Note that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ is just the length of the interval $[2,8],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+({x}_{3}-{x}_{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}}-{x}_{0})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{x}_{3}}-\\cancel{{x}_{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}+{x}_{m} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}-{x}_{0} \\\\  & =8-2 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523971 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186523902 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523971 #edb/ref 1069 "q-122994" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523971 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523971 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $P=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[1,10].$ If $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}2({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523971 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "785f4fec-653e-532c-a878-3835d225527c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523971 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the constant multiple rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}2({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}=2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}.\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the summation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})Δ{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})Δ{x}_{2}+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})Δ{x}_{m} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${x}_{0}=1$ and ${x}_{m}=10$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={10}^{2}-{1}^{2} \\\\  & =99.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}=2\\cdot 99=198.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523978 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186523868 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523978 #edb/ref 1069 "q-122930" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523978 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523978 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[4,8]?$\n\nI. $4<6<8$\n\nII. $5<6<7<8$\n\nIII. $4<5<6<7$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523978 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "84a42ed7-7cdb-52df-a889-40521b20e8c1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523978 #edb/ref 1074 "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na={x}_{0}<{x}_{1}<{x}_{2}<…<{x}_{n}=b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{n}\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is a partition of $[4,8].$\n\n- Statement II is not a partition of $[4,8]$ since it does not include the left endpoint $a=4.$\n\n- Statement III is not a partition of $[4,8]$ since it does not include the right endpoint $b=8.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523983 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186523907 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523983 #edb/ref 1069 "q-122993" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523983 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523983 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $P=\\{{z}_{0},{z}_{1},…,{z}_{q}\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[2,6].$ If $Δ{z}_{k}={z}_{k}-{z}_{k-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}\\frac{({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})}{2}Δ{z}_{k}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523983 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8a05e0a6-f018-5eeb-9fa0-754bde9f9f75" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523983 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the constant multiple rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}\\frac{({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})}{2}Δ{z}_{k}=\\frac{1}{2}{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k}.\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the summation as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k} & =({z}_{1}+{z}_{0})Δ{z}_{1}+({z}_{2}+{z}_{1})Δ{z}_{2}+⋯+({z}_{q}+{z}_{q-1})Δ{z}_{n} \\\\  & =({z}_{1}+{z}_{0})({z}_{1}-{z}_{0})+({z}_{2}+{z}_{1})({z}_{2}-{z}_{1})+⋯+({z}_{q}+{z}_{q-1})({z}_{q}-{z}_{q-1}) \\\\  & =({z}_{1}^{2}-{z}_{0}^{2})+({z}_{2}^{2}-{z}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({z}_{q}^{2}-{z}_{q-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{z}_{1}^{2}}-{z}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{z}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{z}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({z}_{q}^{2}-\\cancel{{z}_{q-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{z}_{0}^{2}+{z}_{q}^{2} \\\\  & ={z}_{q}^{2}-{z}_{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${z}_{0}=2$ and ${z}_{q}=6$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k} & ={z}_{q}^{2}-{z}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={6}^{2}-{2}^{2} \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k}=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 32=16.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524022 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186523811 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524022 #edb/ref 1069 "q-122934" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524022 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524022 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[0,6]?$\n\nI. $0<2<4<8$\n\nII. $\\{0,3,6\\}$\n\nIII. $0<1<3<5<6$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524022 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e49f5076-911d-5cdf-8140-a000de972953" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524022 #edb/ref 1074 "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na={x}_{0}<{x}_{1}<{x}_{2}<…<{x}_{n}=b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{n}\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is not a partition of $[0,6]$ since $8$ does not belong to $[0,6].$\n\n- Statement II is a partition of $[0,6].$\n\n- Statement III is a partition of $[0,6].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524036 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186523796 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524036 #edb/ref 1069 "q-122971" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524036 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524036 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $P=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[-5,5].$ If $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524036 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f1ddbd77-4be4-59b3-aa0d-217f8714ae20" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524036 #edb/ref 1074 "Note that ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}$ is just the length of the interval $[-5,5],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =({y}_{1}-{y}_{0})+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})+({y}_{3}-{y}_{2})+⋯+({y}_{n}-{y}_{n-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{y}_{1}}-{y}_{0})+(\\cancel{{y}_{2}}-\\cancel{{y}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{y}_{3}}-\\cancel{{y}_{2}})+⋯+({y}_{n}-\\cancel{{y}_{n-1}}) \\\\  & =-{y}_{0}+{y}_{n} \\\\  & ={y}_{n}-{y}_{0} \\\\  & =5-(-5) \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
